L263: The PEDro scale is based on the Delphi list developed by Verhage et al. at the Department of Epidemiology, University of Maastricht.[58] Only criteria 2-11 are scored, for a maximum total of 10: 1 eligibility criteria, 2 randomization, 3 concealed allocation, 4 groups similar at baseline, 5 blinding subjects, 6 blinding therapists, 7 blinding assessors, 8 measures obtained for > 85%, 9 intention to treat, 10 between-group statistical comparison, 11 point measures of variability.
